## Overview

The files of a Tuff workspace: documents, screenshots, clipboard exports and themes that sync between the devices you sign in on, plus a Plugin storage partition with one folder per plugin. Its limits are the host's real ones: at most 10 MB per file, 100 MB in total and 1,000 files, no sub-folders, and names made of letters, digits and `. _ -` only.

It fits any "tree + files + preview" interface: synced drives and cloud storage, asset libraries, the data folders of an app or plugin, ticket attachments.

- Selecting: click selects, ⌘ / Ctrl click adds, Shift click extends, ⌘ / Ctrl + A selects everything; the arrow keys move by row and column (the row length is read off the grid itself), Shift + arrows extend, Esc clears. These keys live on the file area and do nothing while focus is elsewhere.
- Opening: double-click or Enter opens a folder or file; Space opens quick look, where ← / → step through the folder and Space or Esc closes it; F2 renames, Enter confirms and Esc cancels, and a plugin storage name that breaks the host's rule is flagged right in place; ⌫ / Delete deletes, with Undo. Download only says what the host would do; nothing is downloaded.
- Right-click, Shift + F10 or the Menu key opens the same menu; from the keyboard it anchors to the focused tile, not to a corner of the whole file area. When it closes, focus goes back to the tile it came from, unless the choice took it on purpose (Rename, Quick look, Move to…). Drag tiles onto a folder in the tree to move them; plugin storage files never move.
- Dragging files in from the desktop shows a drop layer over the file area; after the drop, the tray under Upload shows each file's progress. A plugin folder turns away a file over 10 MB, one that would take the plugin past 100 MB and a name outside the rule, and offers Save to workspace. Images get a thumbnail, and text files up to 256 KB can be previewed. Dropping anywhere else in the template is refused, so the browser never navigates to the file; everything lives in browser memory and is gone when you leave the page.
- The first time the stage scrolls into view the tray says two screenshots are syncing from a MacBook; about 2 seconds later they appear in Screenshots / 2026-09 marked New, and the tray settles away unless the pointer is on it. With reduced motion both files are there from the start and no tray appears.
- In the docs column the layout is a 208px tree beside the file area; expanded (≥ 960px) the tree is 240px, tiles grow and New folder joins the toolbar, and from 1200px the preview pane appears too; below 640px the tree hides, sub-folders show up as tiles and the path keeps only the last crumb, a back button and a parents menu.

## Customization

- For real storage, replace the simulated progress with the upload request's progress events. TxFileUploader only receives `File` objects; keep validation in the host, sharing one set of constants with the host's real limits so the two sides never disagree.
- For very large folders, turn the grid into a virtual list grouped by rows (tiles per row come from the container width), and keep the list view on TxDataTable's controlled sorting with server-side paging.
- For search across folders, show the results as a temporary virtual folder with each item's path, rather than expanding a trail of folders in the tree.
- When thumbnails come from a server, keep the tile height fixed and images `draggable="false"` so the grid does not jump while they load; revoke object URLs on delete, reset and unmount.

